Object.assign(window.IND_FEED_BODY, {"hp-fk.bastar-chariot-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bastar-chariot:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot the Whole Forest Pulls","text":"\"इस उत्सव के केंद्र में चलता है रथ: ठोस लकड़ी और बड़े-बड़े पहियों वाला एक भारी-भरकम रथ, जो किसी घर जितना ऊँचा होता है — और इसे हर साल बिल्कुल नया बनाया जाता है। पूरे विधि-विधान से जंगल से पेड़ लाए जाते हैं, और खास गाँवों के पुश्तैनी बढ़ई परिवार अपने हाथों के औज़ारों से इन्हें गढ़ते हैं, ठीक वैसे ही जैसे उनके बाप-दादा करते आए थे। हर गाँव उस काम को सँभालता है जो पीढ़ियों से उसका सम्मान रहा है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"At its heart rolls the rath: a massive chariot of solid wood on great solid wheels, tall as a house — built completely new each year. Trees are brought from the forest with due ceremony, and hereditary carpenter families from particular villages shape them with hand tools, as their fathers and grandfathers did, each village keeping the task that has been its honour for generations.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bastar-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bastar-chariot|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bastar-chariot-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bastar-chariot:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot the Whole Forest Pulls","text":"\"फिर बारी आती है रथ खींचने की। न कोई इंजन, न कोई जानवर। लंबी, भारी रस्सियाँ — और मुरिया तथा अन्य आदिवासी समुदायों के सैकड़ों नौजवान, जो रथ खींचने का पुश्तैनी हक़ लेकर गाँवों से आते हैं और रस्सियों पर अपनी-अपनी जगह सँभाल लेते हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"Then comes the pulling. No engine, no animals. Long, heavy ropes — and hundreds of young men of the Adivasi communities, Muria and others, who come in from the villages holding the hereditary right to pull the rath, take their places on the lines.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bastar-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bastar-chariot|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bastar-chariot-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bastar-chariot:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot the Whole Forest Pulls","text":"\"कई दिनों तक जगदलपुर की गलियों में बड़े-बड़े पहिए चरचराते हुए घूमते हैं, रस्सियाँ खींचने वालों के हाथ कसे होते हैं, भारी भीड़ उमड़ती है और हवा में नगाड़ों की गूंज भर जाती है। इस त्योहार के कई पड़ाव होते हैं, जिनके अपने-अपने नाम और रीति-रिवाज़ हैं, जो महीनों तक चलते हैं — और इस पूरे समय, देवी का मान-सम्मान बारी-बारी से हर समाज मिलकर संभालता है, उतनी ही हिफ़ाज़त से जितनी हिफ़ाज़त से रथ को खींचा जाता है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"For days the great wheels groan around the streets of Jagdalpur, the ropes taut with hauliers, the crowds vast, the air full of drums. The festival's many stages have their own names and rites, months of them — and through it all, the goddess's honour is carried by turns, community by community, as carefully as the chariot itself.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bastar-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bastar-chariot|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bastar-chariot-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bastar-chariot:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot the Whole Forest Pulls","text":"\"एक मशहूर रात तो ऐसी भी होती है, जिसे कार्यक्रम में सुनते ही हर बच्चा खुश हो जाता है, जब रथ को चुपके से ले जाकर रस्म के तौर पर \"चुरा\" लिया जाता है — और फिर मान-मनौव्वल और दावत के साथ उसे ढूंढकर वापस लाना पड़ता है। बस्तर में यह त्योहार इतने ज़माने से मनाया जा रहा है कि पूजा-पाठ के विधान में भी हँसी-मज़ाक रच-बस गया है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"There is even a famous night, beloved of every child who hears the schedule, when the rath is spirited away and ceremonially \"stolen\" — and must be found and brought back with negotiation and feasting. Bastar has been running this festival so long it has built comedy into the liturgy.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bastar-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bastar-chariot|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.bastar-chariot-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.bastar-chariot:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Chariot the Whole Forest Pulls","text":"\"जब सब पूरा हो जाता है, तो देवी को अगले साल तक के लिए आदर सहित विदा किया जाता है, रथ का काम पूरा हो जाता है, और बढ़इयों के गाँवों को पहले से पता होता है कि अगले साल जंगल नए पेड़ देगा और उनके हाथ फिर से यह सब नया बनाएँगे। कुछ भी सहेजकर नहीं रखा जाता। हर चीज़ नए सिरे से बनती है। यही बस्तर का तरीका है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"When it all ends, the Devi is seen off with honour until the next year, the rath's duty is done, and the carpenter villages already know that next year the forest will give new trees and their hands will build it all again. Nothing is stored. Everything is renewed. That is the Bastar way.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-bastar-chariot.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.bastar-chariot|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.myna-judge-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.myna-judge:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Myna Who Judged the Quarrel","text":"\"छत्तीसगढ़ के बस्तर के जंगलों में चमकीले काले रंग की एक चिड़िया रहती है, जिसके कानों के पास चटख पीले निशान होते हैं, जिसे पहाड़ी मैना कहते हैं — और उसके पास एक मशहूर हुनर है। वह जो भी आवाज़ सुनती है, हूबहू वैसी ही आवाज़ निकाल सकती है। छत्तीसगढ़ उसे इतना प्यार करता है कि उसने उसे अपना राजकीय पक्षी बना लिया। यह कहानी उसी के सम्मान में सुनाई जाती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"In the forests of Bastar, in Chhattisgarh, lives a glossy black bird with bright yellow wattles called the hill myna — and she has one famous gift. She can repeat, perfectly, any voice she hears. Chhattisgarh loves her so well it made her the state bird. This is a fable told in her honour.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-myna-judge.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.myna-judge|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.myna-judge-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.myna-judge:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Myna Who Judged the Quarrel","text":"\"जंगल से लगे एक गाँव के किनारे आम का एक पेड़ था, और उस पेड़ के दोनों तरफ दो पड़ोसी रहते थे, और उनके बीच एक झगड़ा चला आ रहा था जो इतना पुराना था मानो उसने वहीं अपना घर बना लिया हो। पेड़ किसका है? आम किसके हैं? हर मौसम में फलों के साथ-साथ यह चीख-पुकार भी लौट आती थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"On the edge of a forest village stood a mango tree, and on either side of the mango tree lived two neighbours, and between them stood a quarrel so old it had practically built its own house. Whose tree? Whose mangoes? Every season the shouting came back with the fruit.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-myna-judge.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.myna-judge|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.myna-judge-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.myna-judge:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Myna Who Judged the Quarrel","text":"उस साल वे इतनी देर तक और इतना ज़ोर-ज़ोर से चिल्लाए कि पूरे जंगल को उनके भाषण मुँह-ज़बानी याद हो गए। और खुद उसी आम के पेड़ पर, बड़े पेशेवर अंदाज़ में ध्यान से सुनती हुई, एक पहाड़ी मैना बैठी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"They shouted so long and loud that year that the whole forest knew the speeches by heart. And in the mango tree itself, listening with professional interest, sat a hill myna.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-myna-judge.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.myna-judge|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.myna-judge-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.myna-judge:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Myna Who Judged the Quarrel","text":"एक सुबह पड़ोसी वहाँ पहुँचे, तो उन्होंने देखा कि मैना सबसे निचली डाली पर किसी मजिस्ट्रेट की तरह इंतज़ार कर रही थी। \"जंगल ने मुझे जज बनाया है,\" उसने बड़े रौबदार अंदाज़ में ऐलान किया — यह आवाज़ उसने गाँव की मुखिया से सीखी थी। \"अपनी-अपनी बात पेश करो। मैं एक-एक शब्द पर गौर करूँगी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"One morning the neighbours arrived to find the myna on the lowest branch, waiting like a magistrate. \"The forest has appointed me judge,\" she announced — in a voice of great authority, which she had borrowed from the village headwoman. \"Present your cases. I will consider every word.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-myna-judge.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.myna-judge|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.myna-judge-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.myna-judge:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Myna Who Judged the Quarrel","text":"पहले पड़ोसी ने अपनी बात रखी, पूरी की पूरी शिकायतों और गरज से भरी हुई। मैना ने अपनी गर्दन तिरछी की और उसकी बात ज्यों-की-त्यों उसे लौटा दी — एक-एक शब्द, हर फुंकार, और ठीक उसी लहजे में निकला, \"और वो आदमी खुद को पड़ोसी कहता है!\" वह खड़ा-खड़ा खुद की ही बातें सुनता रहा, और धीरे-धीरे उसके कान लाल होते गए।","lang":"hi","body":"The first neighbour gave his speech, all grievance and thunder. The myna cocked her head and gave it back to him — every word, every snort, the exact curl of \"and THAT man calls himself a neighbour!\" He stood there hearing himself, and his ears slowly went red.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-myna-judge.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.myna-judge|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.myna-judge-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.myna-judge:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Myna Who Judged the Quarrel","text":"दूसरी पड़ोसन का हाल भी कुछ बेहतर न रहा। उसका अपना भाषण, जिसे मैना ने हूबहू दोहरा दिया था — उसने अब जाकर गौर किया — उसमें तीन ताने थे, पेड़ जितना बड़ा एक बतंगड़ था, और आमों के बारे में तो कोई बात ही नहीं थी। मैना अपनी चमकीली आँखों से देखती हुई इंतज़ार करती रही, दूसरों की बातों को दोहराने के अलावा वह पूरी तरह खामोश थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The second neighbour fared no better. Her own speech, returned with perfect fidelity, contained — she now noticed — three insults, one exaggeration the size of the tree itself, and nothing whatsoever about mangoes. The myna waited, bright-eyed, entirely silent except for other people's words.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-myna-judge.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.myna-judge|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.myna-judge-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.myna-judge:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Myna Who Judged the Quarrel","text":"अब वे करते भी क्या? खुद को सुनना बड़ी असरदार दवा साबित हुआ। उन दोनों ने पेड़ की जड़ों के आर-पार एक-दूसरे को देखा, शर्मिंदा होकर आखिरकार सच्चाई पर आ ही गए, और पूरे दस मिनट में मामला सुलझा लिया: पेड़ किसी का नहीं था और फल सबके थे, ठीक आधे-आधे बाँटे जाएँगे, और एक टोकरी जज के लिए होगी।","lang":"hi","body":"What could they do? Hearing yourself is a strong medicine. The two of them looked at each other over the roots, embarrassed into honesty at last, and settled the matter in ten minutes flat: the tree was nobody's and the fruit was everybody's, shared down the middle, with a basket for the judge.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-myna-judge.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.myna-judge|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.agaria-first-fire-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.agaria-first-fire:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The People of the First Furnace","text":"छत्तीसगढ़ और मध्य भारत के पहाड़ी इलाकों में अगरिया लोग रहते हैं — एक ऐसा समुदाय जिसके नाम में ही आग बसी है, क्योंकि कई भाषाओं की तरह उनकी बोली में भी 'आग' का मतलब आग ही होता है। अनगिनत सदियों से अगरिया ही लोहा बनाने वाले रहे हैं: ऐसे लोग जो धरती से काला पत्थर निकालते हैं और कोयले, धौंकनी तथा अपनी समझ-बूझ से उसे धातु बनने के लिए मना लेते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Across the hill country of Chhattisgarh and central India live the Agaria — a community whose very name carries fire in it, for ag is fire in their tongue as in many. For centuries beyond reckoning, the Agaria have been the iron-makers: the people who take dark stone out of the earth and, with charcoal and bellows and knowledge, persuade it to become metal.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-agaria-first-fire.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.agaria-first-fire|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.agaria-first-fire-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.agaria-first-fire:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The People of the First Furnace","text":"अगरिया लोगों की समझ में 'मनाना' ही सही शब्द है। उनके लिए लोहा कोई बेजान चीज़ नहीं है। उनकी परंपरा मानती है कि भट्टी में लोहासुर बसते हैं — लोहे के देवता, धातु के स्वामी — और उनका आदर किए बिना लोहा गलाने का काम शुरू नहीं होता। भट्टी के सामने कोई यूँ ही बेपरवाह नहीं चला आता। पहले वहाँ रहने वाले को प्रणाम किया जाता है।","lang":"hi","body":"Persuade is the right word, in the Agaria understanding. Iron is not a dead thing to them. In the furnace, their tradition holds, dwells Lohasur — the iron spirit, the lord of the metal — and no smelting begins without honouring him first. You do not barge into a forge. You greet the one who lives there.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-agaria-first-fire.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.agaria-first-fire|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.agaria-first-fire-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.agaria-first-fire:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The People of the First Furnace","text":"जहाँ आज भी यह पुराना हुनर बचा है, वहाँ इसे देखिए: मिट्टी की एक छोटी सी भट्टी जो खड़े हुए इंसान जैसी बनाई जाती है, जिसमें कच्चे लोहे के पत्थरों और कोयले की परतें भरी होती हैं; घंटों तक एक लय में चलती बकरे की खाल की धौंकनी, जो आग के लिए साँसें भरती है; और फिर वह पल आता है — जब भट्टी खोली जाती है, और जो कभी पत्थर था, उसमें से असली लोहे का दहकता हुआ गोला बाहर निकलता है, किसी नए जन्मे जीव की तरह फुफकारता हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"Watch the old craft, where it survives: a small clay furnace built like a standing person, packed with layers of ore and charcoal; the goat-skin bellows worked in rhythm for hours, breathing for the fire; and then the moment — the furnace opened, and out of what was stone comes a glowing sponge of real iron, hissing like something being born.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-agaria-first-fire.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.agaria-first-fire|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.agaria-first-fire-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.agaria-first-fire:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The People of the First Furnace","text":"एक अगरिया बुज़ुर्ग जब एक लड़के को धौंकनी चलाना सिखा रहे थे, तब लड़के ने उनसे पूछा कि काम शुरू करने से पहले वे हर बार आग और लोहे का धन्यवाद क्यों करते हैं, जबकि उनका परिवार दसियों हज़ार बार यह काम कर चुका है।","lang":"hi","body":"An Agaria elder, teaching a boy the bellows, was asked by him why they thank the fire and the iron before beginning, every single time, when the family has done this ten thousand times.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-agaria-first-fire.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.agaria-first-fire|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.agaria-first-fire-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.agaria-first-fire:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The People of the First Furnace","text":"और ज़रा सोचिए कि उस समझौते ने बाकी सबको क्या दिया। किसान के हल का फाल, कुल्हाड़ी, हँसिया, तीर की नोक, हाँडी की तिपाई — सदियों तक मध्य भारत के गाँव अगरिया लोहे के दम पर ही चलते रहे। गाँव के छोर पर भट्टी के पास बैठा वह शांत परिवार दुनिया का आधा काम सँभाले हुए था।","lang":"hi","body":"And think what that agreement gave everyone else. The farmer's ploughshare, the axe, the sickle, the arrowhead, the cooking pot's stand — for centuries, the villages of central India ran on Agaria iron. The quiet family at the furnace on the village edge was holding up half the world's work.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-agaria-first-fire.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.agaria-first-fire|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.agaria-first-fire-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.agaria-first-fire:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The People of the First Furnace","text":"पहली भट्टी और पहले लोहे के बारे में अगरिया लोगों की अपनी कहानियाँ बड़ी समृद्ध हैं — लोहासुर, पहले लुहारों, और आग व इंसानों के बीच हुए कड़े समझौतों से भरी हुईं। पीढ़ियों पहले विद्वानों ने इनमें से कुछ को लिख लिया था; पर समुदाय के बुज़ुर्ग ही इनके सच्चे रखवाले हैं, और जैसा कि हर जीती-जागती परंपरा में होता है, गाँव-गाँव के साथ इन कहानियों के रंग बदलते जाते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The Agaria's own tellings of the first furnace and the first iron are theirs, and they are rich — full of the iron spirit, the first smiths, and hard bargains between fire and people. Scholars wrote some of them down generations ago; the community's own elders remain the true keepers, and versions differ village to village, as living lore does.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-agaria-first-fire.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.agaria-first-fire|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.agaria-first-fire-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.agaria-first-fire:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The People of the First Furnace","text":"अब भारत का लोहा बड़े-बड़े कारखानों में बनता है, और मिट्टी की पुरानी भट्ठियाँ बहुत कम बची हैं। लेकिन यह हुनर कि कोई नदी किनारे की मिट्टी से भट्ठी बना ले और पत्थर में फूँक मारकर धातु निकाल ले — वह आज भी वहीं बसता है जहाँ हमेशा से था: अगरिया लोगों की यादों में, और उन हाथों में जो छोटों को दिखाने के लिए आज भी पुरानी तरह से लोहा गलाते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Big mills make India's iron now, and the old clay furnaces are few. But the knowledge that a person can build a furnace from riverbank clay and breathe stone into metal — that lives where it always lived: in Agaria memory, and in the hands of those who still demonstrate the old smelting for the young to see.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-agaria-first-fire.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.agaria-first-fire|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chitrakote-sings-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chitrakote-sings:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Waterfall That Sings","text":"छत्तीसगढ़ के बस्तर में, इंद्रावती नदी घोड़े की नाल जैसी चट्टान तक पहुँचती है और एक साथ नीचे छलाँग लगा देती है। गिरते पानी की यह चादर इतनी चौड़ी है कि लोग चित्रकोट को भारत का सबसे चौड़ा झरना कहते हैं — देश का अपना छोटा नयाग्रा, जो हमेशा धुंध का दुपट्टा ओढ़े रहता है।","lang":"hi","body":"In Bastar, in Chhattisgarh, the Indravati river comes to a horseshoe-shaped cliff and steps off it, all at once, in a curtain of falling water so wide that people call Chitrakote the widest waterfall in India — the country's own little Niagara, wearing a permanent scarf of mist.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chitrakote-sings.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chitrakote-sings|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chitrakote-sings-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chitrakote-sings:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Waterfall That Sings","text":"आस-पास के गाँवों के लोग हमेशा से इस झरने के साथ रहे हैं, और वे तुम्हें वही बात बताएँगे जो हर मुसाफ़िर को देर-सवेर समझ आती है: चित्रकोट की आवाज़ कभी एक जैसी नहीं रहती। जैसे इंसानों की आवाज़ बदलती है, वैसे ही इसके सुरों के भी मौसम होते हैं। नदी किनारे रहने वाले एक दादाजी ने अपनी पोती को इसी के बारे में यह बात बताई थी।","lang":"hi","body":"The villages of the country around have lived with the falls forever, and they will tell you what every visitor eventually notices: Chitrakote never sounds the same twice. It has seasons of voice, as a person does. This is the telling one riverside grandfather gave his granddaughter about that.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chitrakote-sings.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chitrakote-sings|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chitrakote-sings-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chitrakote-sings:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Waterfall That Sings","text":"\"बरसात में,\" उन्होंने कहा, \"वह किसी भीड़ जैसी होती है — पूरा मटमैला पानी एक साथ किनारे से गरजता हुआ गिरता है, और उसके पास अपनी बात सुनाने के लिए तुम्हें भी चिल्लाना पड़ता है। शरद में वह उजली होकर कई सुरों में गाती है। और सूखे के महीनों में वह सिमटकर चाँदी के धागों जैसी हो जाती है, और दावत के बाद बजने वाली बाँसुरी की तरह धीमे-धीमे बहती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"In the monsoon,\" he said, \"she is a crowd — the whole brown flood shouting over the edge at once, and you must shout too, to be heard beside her. In autumn she is a choir, white and many-voiced. And in the dry months she narrows to silver threads, and plays soft, like a flute at the end of a feast.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chitrakote-sings.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chitrakote-sings|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chitrakote-sings-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chitrakote-sings:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Waterfall That Sings","text":"बच्ची ने एक बड़ा अच्छा सवाल पूछा: \"इतने सारे गाने क्यों? चट्टानें तो पूरे साल वही की वही रहती हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"The girl asked the good question: \"Why so many songs? The rocks are the same rocks all year.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chitrakote-sings.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chitrakote-sings|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chitrakote-sings-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chitrakote-sings:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Waterfall That Sings","text":"\"लोग भी बिल्कुल ऐसे ही होते हैं,\" बूढ़े दादाजी ने बात आगे बढ़ाई, क्योंकि दादाजी लोग झरने का मौका कभी खाली नहीं जाने देते। \"शोरगुल के मौसम, खामोश मौसम, भरे-पूरे साल और तंगी के दिन — और इन सब के पीछे इंसान वही का वही। किसी के शांत महीने को उसका पूरा संगीत समझने की भूल मत करना।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"People are the same,\" the old man added, since a grandfather never wastes a waterfall. \"Loud seasons, soft seasons, full years and lean ones — and the same person underneath all of it. Do not mistake somebody's quiet month for their whole music.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chitrakote-sings.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chitrakote-sings|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chitrakote-sings-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chitrakote-sings:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Waterfall That Sings","text":"इंद्रावती बस्तर की सबसे बड़ी नदी है — अपने पूरे रास्ते में बसे लोगों को खेत और मछलियाँ देने वाली — और यह झरना उसका सबसे भव्य रूप है। पूर्णिमा की रातों में झरने के ऊपर उठती धुंध चांदी जैसी चमकने लगती है, और नीचे के कुंड चाँद को किसी सिक्के की तरह संभाल लेते हैं, और किसी को भी घर लौटने की जल्दी नहीं होती।","lang":"hi","body":"The Indravati is Bastar's great river — the giver of fields and fish for the communities along her whole length — and the falls are her grandest public appearance. On full-moon nights the mist over the drop goes silver, and the pools below hold the moon like a coin, and nobody hurries home.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chitrakote-sings.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chitrakote-sings|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.chitrakote-sings-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.chitrakote-sings:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Waterfall That Sings","text":"अब दुनिया भर से मुसाफ़िर कैमरे लिए आते हैं, और गाँव वाले उन्हें चाय बेचते हैं और एक-एक करके उन्हें वही राज़ पाते देखते हैं जो बस्तर हमेशा से जानता था: चित्रकूट की सिर्फ़ तस्वीर नहीं उतारी जा सकती। आप उसकी फुहारों में खड़े होते हैं, और वह जिस भी मौसम का गीत साध रही हो उसे गाने देते हैं, और बदले में वही अपने साथ घर ले जाते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Travellers come now from across the world with cameras, and the villages sell them tea and watch them discover, one by one, what Bastar always knew: you do not really photograph Chitrakote. You stand in the spray and let her sing whichever season's song she is practising, and you take that home instead.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-chitrakote-sings.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.chitrakote-sings|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.danteshwari-bastar-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.danteshwari-bastar:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess Who Walked Behind","text":"दक्षिणी छत्तीसगढ़ के विशाल जंगलों की धरती बस्तर की एक माँ हैं: दंतेश्वरी। इस इलाके का हर समुदाय — गाँव और शहर, जंगल और खेत — उन्हें इस धरती की अपनी देवी मानकर पूजता है, और उनका मुख्य मंदिर दंतेवाड़ा में है, जहाँ दो नदियाँ मिलती हैं। यह उनके आगमन की कथा है, ठीक वैसी ही जैसी बस्तर में सुनाई जाती है।","lang":"hi","body":"Bastar, the great forest land of southern Chhattisgarh, has a mother: Danteshwari. Every community of the region — village and town, forest and field — honours her as the land's own goddess, and her chief temple stands at Dantewada, where two rivers meet. This is the katha of how she came, told as Bastar tells it.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-danteshwari-bastar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.danteshwari-bastar|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.danteshwari-bastar-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.danteshwari-bastar:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess Who Walked Behind","text":"कहा जाता है कि बहुत समय पहले, अन्नमदेव नाम के एक राजा अपना पुराना राज्य छोड़कर दक्षिण के जंगलों में एक नया राज्य बसाने जा रहे थे। रवाना होने से पहले, उन्होंने उसी देवी की प्रार्थना की जिनकी सेवा उनका परिवार हमेशा से करता आया था — और देवी ने उन्हें एक वचन दिया, और साथ में एक शर्त भी, और देवियों के वचन आम तौर पर ऐसे ही मिला करते हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"Long ago, the telling goes, a king called Annamdeva was leaving his old kingdom to found a new one in the southern forests. Before he set out, he prayed to the goddess his family had always served — and she gave him a promise, and a condition, which is how promises from goddesses usually arrive.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-danteshwari-bastar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.danteshwari-bastar|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.danteshwari-bastar-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.danteshwari-bastar:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess Who Walked Behind","text":"\"मैं आपके साथ चलूँगी,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"मैं आपके पीछे-पीछे चलूँगी, और जहाँ-जहाँ मेरे क़दम पड़ेंगे, वहीं आपका राज्य होगा। आप मुझे देख नहीं पाएँगे — लेकिन हर क़दम पर, अपने पीछे आपको मेरी पायलों की आवाज़ सुनाई देगी। आगे बढ़ते रहिए, और उस आवाज़ पर भरोसा रखिए। और पीछे मुड़कर मुझे मत देखिएगा। बस यही एक शर्त है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"I will come with you,\" she said. \"I will walk behind you, and where my feet go, your kingdom will be. You will not see me — but you will hear my anklets at your back, every step. Walk ahead, and trust the sound. And do not look back at me. That is the whole of the condition.\"","art":"art/story/sm/fk-danteshwari-bastar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.danteshwari-bastar|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.danteshwari-bastar-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.danteshwari-bastar:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess Who Walked Behind","text":"तो राजा कई दिनों तक दक्षिण की ओर चलते रहे, जंगलों और पहाड़ियों को पार करते हुए — और उनके पीछे-पीछे हमेशा, छम, छम, पायलों की वही चाँदी जैसी आवाज़ गूँजती रही, उनकी अपनी दिल की धड़कन की तरह नियमित। जब तक कि वे उस जगह नहीं पहुँच गए जहाँ दो नदियाँ मिलती हैं, और जैसे ही उन्होंने उथले पानी में क़दम रखा — वह आवाज़ थम गई।","lang":"hi","body":"So the king walked south, day upon day, through forests and over hills — and always behind him, chham, chham, the silver sound of the anklets, steady as his own heartbeat. Until he came to a place where two rivers meet, and crossed into the shallows, and there — the sound stopped.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-danteshwari-bastar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.danteshwari-bastar|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.danteshwari-bastar-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.danteshwari-bastar:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess Who Walked Behind","text":"शर्त टूट चुकी थी, और देवी वहीं रुक गईं जहाँ राजा की नज़र उन पर पड़ी थी। \"यहाँ तक मैं चलकर आई,\" उन्होंने कहा, \"और इतना ही बहुत है। यहाँ, जहाँ नदियाँ मिलती हैं, मैं यहीं रहूँगी — और यहीं से मैं आपकी पूरी धरती को सँभालूँगी।\" कहानी सुनाने वाले ज़ोर देकर कहते हैं कि इसमें ज़रा भी ग़ुस्सा नहीं था। देवी तो किसी टूटी हुई शर्त को भी एक सुंदर आशीर्वाद में बदल देती हैं।","lang":"hi","body":"The condition was broken, and the goddess stayed where his glance had found her. \"This far I have walked,\" she said, \"and this far is enough. Here, where the rivers meet, I remain — and from here I will hold your whole land.\" There was no anger in it, the tellers insist. A goddess turns even a broken condition into a blessing with a good address.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-danteshwari-bastar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.danteshwari-bastar|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.danteshwari-bastar-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.danteshwari-bastar:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess Who Walked Behind","text":"और इसीलिए दंतेश्वरी का मंदिर आज भी दंतेवाड़ा में, शंखिनी और डंकिनी नाम की नदियों के संगम पर शान से खड़ा है, ठीक उसी जगह जहाँ पायलें ख़ामोश हुई थीं — और उस नगर का नाम भी उन्हीं के नाम पर पड़ा। राजा ने अपना राज्य उन्हीं के इर्द-गिर्द बसाया, और शुरू से उस वचन का यही तो असली मतलब था।","lang":"hi","body":"And so the temple of Danteshwari stands to this day at Dantewada, at the meeting of the rivers called Shankhini and Dankini, on the very spot where the anklets fell silent — and the town itself bears her name. The king built his kingdom around her, which is what the promise had meant all along.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-danteshwari-bastar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.danteshwari-bastar|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-fk.danteshwari-bastar-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:fk.danteshwari-bastar:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Goddess Who Walked Behind","text":"हर साल बस्तर दशहरे के पचहत्तर दिनों के महापर्व पर, दंतेश्वरी को पूरे आदर के साथ जगदलपुर लाया जाता है, और पूरा बस्तर उनके पास जुटता है। उस धरती का यह सबसे भव्य उत्सव उसी देवी के चारों ओर घूमता है, जो कभी अपने पैरों में चाँदी की पायलें पहने एक राजा के पीछे चली थीं।","lang":"hi","body":"Each year at Bastar Dussehra, the great seventy-five-day festival, Danteshwari is brought with honour to Jagdalpur, and all Bastar gathers to her. The whole festival, grandest in the land, turns around the goddess who once walked behind a king with silver at her ankles.","art":"art/story/sm/fk-danteshwari-bastar.jpg","route":"#/story/fk.danteshwari-bastar|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","The Heart of the Land"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.lion-rabbit-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.lion-rabbit:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lion Who Met Himself","text":"मंदार के जंगल में भासुरक नाम का एक शेर रहता था। वह भूखा नहीं था। मुश्किल यही थी। वह मज़े के लिए मारता था — दिन में दस जानवर — और जंगल ख़ाली होता जा रहा था।","lang":"hi","body":"In the forest of Mandara there lived a lion called Bhasuraka. He was not hungry. That was the trouble. He killed for the fun of it, ten animals a day, and the forest was emptying out.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-lion-rabbit.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.lion-rabbit|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.lion-rabbit-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.lion-rabbit:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lion Who Met Himself","text":"“महाराज,” काँपते हुए सब जानवरों ने कहा, “हमारा शिकार करना बंद कीजिए। हम हर दिन आपके पास एक जानवर भेज देंगे। आपको पंजा भी नहीं उठाना पड़ेगा।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"Great king,\" said the animals, trembling together, \"stop hunting us. We will send you one animal every single day. You will never have to lift a paw.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-lion-rabbit.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.lion-rabbit|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.lion-rabbit-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.lion-rabbit:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lion Who Met Himself","text":"“ठीक है,” भासुरक ने जम्हाई लेते हुए कहा। “पर जिस दिन कोई नहीं आया — उस दिन मैं तुम सबको खा जाऊँगा।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"Agreed,\" yawned Bhasuraka. \"But if one day nobody comes — I will eat every last one of you.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-lion-rabbit.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.lion-rabbit|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.lion-rabbit-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.lion-rabbit:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lion Who Met Himself","text":"और ऐसे ही चलता रहा। हर दिन एक जानवर, अपनी ही मौत की ओर चलता हुआ। फिर एक दिन बारी आई एक बहुत छोटे, बहुत धीमे, बहुत सोचने वाले ख़रगोश की।","lang":"hi","body":"And so it went. One animal each day, walking to its own death. Until the day the lot fell to a very small, very slow, very thoughtful rabbit.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-lion-rabbit.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.lion-rabbit|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.lion-rabbit-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.lion-rabbit:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lion Who Met Himself","text":"“मैं छोटा हूँ,” ख़रगोश ने ख़ुद से कहा, जितना धीरे चल सकता था उतना धीरे चलते हुए। “मैं उससे लड़ नहीं सकता। मैं उससे भाग नहीं सकता। पर सोचने के लिए मेरे पास पूरी सुबह है — और उसके पास बिलकुल नहीं।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"I am small,\" said the rabbit to himself, walking as slowly as he possibly could. \"I cannot fight him. I cannot outrun him. But I have all morning to think — and he has none.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-lion-rabbit.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.lion-rabbit|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.lion-rabbit-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.lion-rabbit:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lion Who Met Himself","text":"“तू देर से आया है!” भासुरक दहाड़ा। “और तू तो एक कौर भी नहीं है!”","lang":"hi","body":"\"YOU ARE LATE!\" roared Bhasuraka. \"And you are barely a mouthful!\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-lion-rabbit.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.lion-rabbit|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.lion-rabbit-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.lion-rabbit:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lion Who Met Himself","text":"“माफ़ कीजिए, महाराज। पाँच ख़रगोश भेजे गए थे। पर रास्ते में दूसरे शेर ने हमें पकड़ लिया और चार को खा गया। वह कहता है कि इस जंगल का असली राजा वही है। उसने कहा कि आप कुछ भी नहीं हैं।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"Forgive me, king. Five rabbits were sent. But another lion caught us on the road and ate four. He said he is the real king of this forest. He said you are nobody.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-lion-rabbit.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.lion-rabbit|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.lion-rabbit-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.lion-rabbit:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lion Who Met Himself","text":"ख़रगोश उसे एक पुराने पत्थर के कुएँ तक ले गया — गहरा और शांत। “वह अंदर रहता है,” उसने धीरे से कहा। भासुरक ने किनारे से झाँका — और वह वहाँ था। दूसरा शेर। सीधे उसकी ओर घूरता हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"The rabbit led him to an old stone well, deep and still. \"He lives in there,\" he whispered. Bhasuraka leaned over the edge — and there he was. The other lion. Glaring straight up at him.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-lion-rabbit.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.lion-rabbit|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.lion-rabbit-9":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.lion-rabbit:9","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Lion Who Met Himself","text":"भासुरक दहाड़ा। कुआँ और ज़ोर से दहाड़ा। तो वह लड़ने के लिए कूद पड़ा। और यही भासुरक का अंत था — जिसने ज़िंदगी में एक बार भी ख़ुद को देखकर यह नहीं समझा कि वह क्या देख रहा है।","lang":"hi","body":"Bhasuraka roared. The well roared back, louder. So he jumped in to fight him. And that was the end of Bhasuraka — who had never once in his life looked at himself and understood what he was seeing.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-lion-rabbit.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.lion-rabbit|h9","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.monkey-crocodile-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.monkey-crocodile:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkey Who Kept His Heart in a Tree","text":"एक चौड़ी नदी के किनारे जामुन का एक पेड़ था, बैंगनी फलों से लदा हुआ। उसी पर एक बंदर रहता था, जिसके पास खाने से कहीं ज़्यादा फल थे — और बाँटने के लिए कोई नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"On the bank of a wide river grew a jamun tree, heavy with purple fruit. In it lived a monkey who had more fruit than he could ever eat, and nobody to share it with.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-monkey-crocodile.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.monkey-crocodile|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.monkey-crocodile-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.monkey-crocodile:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkey Who Kept His Heart in a Tree","text":"एक दिन एक मगरमच्छ किनारे पर सुस्ताने चढ़ आया। “तुम थके लग रहे हो,” बंदर ने कहा, और मुट्ठी भर जामुन नीचे गिरा दिए। “ये चखो।”","lang":"hi","body":"One day a crocodile hauled himself up onto the bank to rest. \"You look tired,\" said the monkey, and dropped him a handful of jamuns. \"Try these.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-monkey-crocodile.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.monkey-crocodile|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.monkey-crocodile-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.monkey-crocodile:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkey Who Kept His Heart in a Tree","text":"दोस्ती वैसे ही हुई जैसे होती है — धीरे-धीरे, फलों के सहारे, महीनों तक हर दोपहर। मगरमच्छ कुछ जामुन अपनी पत्नी के लिए भी ले जाने लगा।","lang":"hi","body":"They became friends the way you do — slowly, over fruit, every afternoon for months. The crocodile started carrying some home to his wife.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-monkey-crocodile.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.monkey-crocodile|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.monkey-crocodile-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.monkey-crocodile:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkey Who Kept His Heart in a Tree","text":"“अगर फल इतने मीठे हैं,” एक शाम उसकी पत्नी बोली, “तो सोचो वह बंदर कैसा होगा। उसने तो ज़िंदगी भर मिठास के सिवा कुछ खाया ही नहीं। मुझे उसका कलेजा चाहिए।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"If the fruit is this sweet,\" his wife said one evening, \"imagine the monkey. He has eaten nothing but sweetness his whole life. I want his heart.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-monkey-crocodile.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.monkey-crocodile|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.monkey-crocodile-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.monkey-crocodile:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkey Who Kept His Heart in a Tree","text":"“वह मेरा दोस्त है,” मगरमच्छ ने कहा। “वह मेरा खाना है,” पत्नी बोली, “वरना मैं तुम्हारी पत्नी नहीं।” और मगरमच्छ — जो ठीक उसी तरह कमज़ोर था जिस तरह की कमज़ोरी जान ले लेती है — पेड़ के पास लौट गया।","lang":"hi","body":"\"He is my friend,\" said the crocodile. \"He is my dinner,\" said his wife, \"or I am not your wife.\" And the crocodile — who was weak in exactly the way that gets people killed — went back to the tree.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-monkey-crocodile.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.monkey-crocodile|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.monkey-crocodile-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.monkey-crocodile:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkey Who Kept His Heart in a Tree","text":"“नदी पार मेरे घर चलो,” उसने कहा। “मेरी पत्नी तुम्हें धन्यवाद कहना चाहती है।” बंदर, जिसे तैरना बिलकुल नहीं आता था, पूरे भरोसे के साथ उसकी पीठ पर चढ़ गया।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Come to my home across the river,\" he said. \"My wife wants to thank you.\" The monkey, who could not swim a stroke, climbed onto his back with total trust.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-monkey-crocodile.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.monkey-crocodile|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.monkey-crocodile-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.monkey-crocodile:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkey Who Kept His Heart in a Tree","text":"बीच नदी में, सबसे गहरे पानी पर, मगरमच्छ रुक गया। “मुझे तुमसे कुछ कहना है,” उसने कहा। “मेरी पत्नी तुम्हारा कलेजा खाना चाहती है।”","lang":"hi","body":"Halfway across, in the deepest water, the crocodile stopped. \"I have to tell you something,\" he said. \"My wife wants to eat your heart.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-monkey-crocodile.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.monkey-crocodile|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.monkey-crocodile-7":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.monkey-crocodile:7","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkey Who Kept His Heart in a Tree","text":"“अरे! यह पहले क्यों नहीं बताया?” बंदर हँस पड़ा। “हम बंदर तो अपना कलेजा पेड़ पर ही टाँगकर रखते हैं। वह बहुत कीमती होता है, साथ लेकर नहीं घूमते। मुझे वापस ले चलो, मैं ले आता हूँ।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"Oh! Why didn't you say so before we left?\" laughed the monkey. \"We monkeys keep our hearts hanging in the tree. It is far too precious to carry about. Take me back and I will fetch it for you.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-monkey-crocodile.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.monkey-crocodile|h7","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.monkey-crocodile-8":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.monkey-crocodile:8","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Monkey Who Kept His Heart in a Tree","text":"और मगरमच्छ — जिसने बंदर की कही हर बात पर हमेशा यकीन किया था, और अब भी न करने की कोई वजह नहीं दिखी — मुड़ा और उसे पूरी नदी पार वापस ले आया।","lang":"hi","body":"And the crocodile — who had believed every word the monkey had ever said, and saw no reason to stop now — turned around and swam him all the way back.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-monkey-crocodile.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.monkey-crocodile|h8","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.talkative-tortoise-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.talkative-tortoise:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Who Had to Have the Last Word","text":"उज्जैन के पास एक झील में कंबुग्रीव नाम का एक कछुआ रहता था, और दो हंस उसके सबसे प्यारे दोस्त थे। कंबुग्रीव में बस एक ही खोट थी। वह बोलना बंद ही नहीं कर पाता था। एक पल के लिए भी नहीं। किसी भी हाल में नहीं।","lang":"hi","body":"In a lake near Ujjain lived a tortoise named Kambugriva, and two geese who were his dearest friends. Kambugriva had exactly one fault. He could not stop talking. Not for a moment. Not for anything.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-talkative-tortoise.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.talkative-tortoise|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.talkative-tortoise-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.talkative-tortoise:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Who Had to Have the Last Word","text":"एक गर्मी में बारिश नहीं हुई। झील सिकुड़कर कीचड़ रह गई। “हमें किसी बड़ी झील तक उड़ना होगा,” हंसों ने कहा। “पर तुम उड़ नहीं सकते, और हम तुम्हें छोड़ नहीं सकते।”","lang":"hi","body":"One summer the rains failed. The lake shrank to mud. \"We must fly to a bigger lake,\" said the geese. \"But you cannot fly, and we cannot leave you.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-talkative-tortoise.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.talkative-tortoise|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.talkative-tortoise-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.talkative-tortoise:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Who Had to Have the Last Word","text":"“मेरे पास एक तरकीब है!” कंबुग्रीव चिल्लाया। “एक लकड़ी ढूँढ़ो। तुम दोनों उसके सिरे अपनी चोंच में पकड़ लेना। मैं बीच में दाँत से पकड़ लूँगा। और हम उड़ चलेंगे।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"I have an idea!\" cried Kambugriva. \"Find a stick. You each hold an end in your beak. I will bite the middle. And we fly.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-talkative-tortoise.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.talkative-tortoise|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.talkative-tortoise-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.talkative-tortoise:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Who Had to Have the Last Word","text":"“चल जाएगा,” हंसों ने धीरे से कहा, “पर एक शर्त पर। तुम कुछ भी देखो, कोई कुछ भी कहे — मुँह मत खोलना। एक बार भी नहीं। वरना गिर जाओगे।”","lang":"hi","body":"\"It will work,\" said the geese slowly, \"on one condition. Whatever you see, whatever anyone says — you must not open your mouth. Not once. You will fall.\"","art":"art/story/sm/pt-talkative-tortoise.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.talkative-tortoise|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.talkative-tortoise-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.talkative-tortoise:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Who Had to Have the Last Word","text":"वे ऊपर उड़ चले। कीचड़ के ऊपर से, खेतों के ऊपर से, सड़क के ऊपर से — और पूरा कस्बा दौड़कर बाहर आ गया, आसमान में उस अजूबे को देखकर उँगली उठाता और चिल्लाता हुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"Up they went. Over the mud, over the fields, over the road — and the whole town came running out to look, pointing and shouting at the astonishing thing in the sky.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-talkative-tortoise.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.talkative-tortoise|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.talkative-tortoise-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.talkative-tortoise:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Tortoise Who Had to Have the Last Word","text":"“वह देखो!” लोग चिल्लाए। “पक्षी कितने चतुर हैं! देखो तो चतुर पक्षियों ने क्या तरकीब निकाली है!” और लकड़ी से लटके कंबुग्रीव के सीने में कुछ गरम-गरम उठने लगा।","lang":"hi","body":"\"Look at that!\" they yelled. \"The birds are so clever! Look what the clever birds have invented!\" And Kambugriva, dangling from his stick, felt something hot rise in his chest.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-talkative-tortoise.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.talkative-tortoise|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.blue-jackal-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.blue-jackal:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Jackal Who Turned Blue","text":"चंडरव नाम का एक भूखा सियार रात को कुछ खाने की तलाश में कस्बे में घुस आया। पहले उसे कुत्तों ने पा लिया। वह भागा — एक फाटक से, एक आँगन से, और सीधे एक रँगरेज़ के बड़े से नील के मटके में जा गिरा।","lang":"hi","body":"A hungry jackal called Chandarava crept into a town at night looking for scraps. The dogs found him first. He ran — through a gate, through a yard, and straight into a dyer's enormous vat.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-blue-jackal.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.blue-jackal|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.blue-jackal-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.blue-jackal:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Jackal Who Turned Blue","text":"सुबह वह टपकता हुआ बाहर निकला, और उसका एक-एक बाल गहरे, चमकते नीले रंग का हो चुका था। जंगल के किसी जानवर ने किसी जीते-जागते प्राणी पर ऐसा रंग कभी नहीं देखा था।","lang":"hi","body":"He climbed out at dawn, dripping, and every hair on him was a deep and glorious indigo blue. No animal in the forest had ever seen such a colour on a living creature.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-blue-jackal.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.blue-jackal|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.blue-jackal-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.blue-jackal:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Jackal Who Turned Blue","text":"“झुक जाओ,” चंडरव ने कहा, जो तेज़ दिमाग़ का था। “मुझे स्वर्ग से तुम्हारा राजा बनाकर भेजा गया है। मेरा रंग देखो। ऐसा रंग कभी देखा है?” किसी ने नहीं देखा था। शेर झुका। बाघ झुका। सब झुक गए।","lang":"hi","body":"\"KNEEL,\" said Chandarava, who was quick. \"I have been sent down from heaven to be your king. Behold my colour. Have you ever seen its like?\" They had not. The lion knelt. The tiger knelt. Everyone knelt.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-blue-jackal.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.blue-jackal|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.blue-jackal-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.blue-jackal:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Jackal Who Turned Blue","text":"उसने बहुत बढ़िया राज किया। शेरों को मंत्री बनाया और बाघों को पहरेदार। और हर सियार को जंगल से बाहर निकाल दिया — क्योंकि सियार तो आम थे और वह ख़ास था, और क्योंकि वे उसे पहचान सकते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"He ruled beautifully. He kept lions as ministers and tigers as guards. And he drove every jackal out of the forest, because jackals were common, and he was not — and because they might recognise him.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-blue-jackal.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.blue-jackal|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-pt.blue-jackal-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:pt.blue-jackal:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Jackal Who Turned Blue","text":"महीनों यही चलता रहा। फिर एक शाम, पेड़ों के बहुत पीछे कहीं, सियारों का एक झुंड चाँद को देखकर हुआँ-हुआँ करने लगा।","lang":"hi","body":"It went on for months. Then one evening, far off beyond the trees, a pack of jackals began to howl at the moon.","art":"art/story/sm/pt-blue-jackal.jpg","route":"#/story/pt.blue-jackal|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Panchatantra"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.shorter-line-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.shorter-line:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Line Nobody Could Shorten","text":"बादशाह अकबर को अपने दरबार के सामने नामुमकिन पहेलियाँ रखना बहुत पसंद था, ख़ास तौर पर इसलिए क्योंकि उन्हें बीरबल को वे पहेलियाँ सुलझाते देखना अच्छा लगता था। एक सुबह उन्होंने चाक के एक टुकड़े से फ़र्श पर एक लंबी लकीर खींच दी।","lang":"hi","body":"The Emperor Akbar liked to set his court impossible problems, mostly because he liked watching Birbal solve them. One morning he drew a long line across the floor with a piece of chalk.","art":"art/story/sm/ab-shorter-line.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.shorter-line|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.shorter-line-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.shorter-line:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Line Nobody Could Shorten","text":"\"इस लकीर को छोटा करो,\" अकबर ने कहा। \"मगर तुम इसका कोई भी हिस्सा मिटा नहीं सकते। तुम इसे बिल्कुल छू भी नहीं सकते।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Make this line shorter,\" said Akbar. \"But you may not rub out any part of it. You may not touch it at all.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ab-shorter-line.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.shorter-line|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.shorter-line-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.shorter-line:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Line Nobody Could Shorten","text":"मंत्री उसके चारों तरफ़ चक्कर लगाने लगे। वे झुककर आँखें सिकोड़ते हुए उसे ग़ौर से देखने लगे। एक ने उसका छोर कपड़े से ढकने की सलाह दी, जिस पर बादशाह ने टोका कि यह भी तो उसे छूना ही हुआ। कोई कुछ भी नहीं कर पाया।","lang":"hi","body":"The ministers walked around it. They crouched down and squinted at it. One suggested covering the end with a cloth, which the Emperor pointed out was still touching it. Nobody could do anything at all.","art":"art/story/sm/ab-shorter-line.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.shorter-line|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.shorter-line-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.shorter-line:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Line Nobody Could Shorten","text":"उन्होंने पहली लकीर के ठीक बगल में एक दूसरी लकीर खींच दी — बहुत, बहुत ज़्यादा लंबी। फिर वे पीछे हटे और झुककर आदाब किया। \"जहाँपनाह, आपकी लकीर अब दोनों में छोटी हो गई है। मैंने तो इसे छुआ भी नहीं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"He drew a second line right beside the first — much, much longer. Then he stepped back and bowed. \"Your line, Jahanpanah, is now the shorter of the two. I did not touch it.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ab-shorter-line.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.shorter-line|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.khichdi-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.khichdi:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Birbal's Khichdi","text":"साल का सबसे ठंडा हफ़्ता चल रहा था। \"एक हज़ार सोने के सिक्के मिलेंगे,\" अकबर ने ऐलान किया, \"उस इंसान को जो बिना आग और बिना कंबल के, सारी रात महल की झील में गले तक पानी में खड़ा रह सके।\"","lang":"hi","body":"It was the coldest week of the year. \"A thousand gold coins,\" announced Akbar, \"to anyone who can stand in the palace lake all night, up to his neck, with no fire and no blanket.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ab-khichdi.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.khichdi|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.khichdi-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.khichdi:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Birbal's Khichdi","text":"एक गरीब आदमी आगे आया। उसे अपने परिवार का पेट भरना था और बेचने के लिए उसके पास कुछ भी नहीं बचा था। सूरज ढलते ही वह उस काले पानी में उतर गया और रात भर थर-थर काँपते हुए वहीं खड़ा रहा, जब तक कि सुबह सूरज नहीं निकल आया।","lang":"hi","body":"A poor man came forward. He had a family to feed and nothing else to sell. He walked into the black water at sunset and stood there, all night, shaking, until the sun came up.","art":"art/story/sm/ab-khichdi.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.khichdi|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.khichdi-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.khichdi:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Birbal's Khichdi","text":"\"तुम ज़िंदा कैसे बच गए?\" अकबर ने पूछा। \"जहाँपनाह, दूर एक खिड़की में एक दीया जल रहा था,\" उस आदमी ने कहा। \"मैं सारी रात उसी को देखता रहा।\" \"तो तुम्हें उस दीये से गर्मी मिल रही थी!\" एक मंत्री बोला। \"इसने बेईमानी की है। कोई इनाम नहीं मिलेगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"How did you survive?\" asked Akbar. \"There was a lamp burning in a window far away, Jahanpanah,\" the man said. \"I looked at it all night.\" \"Then you were warmed by the lamp!\" said a minister. \"He cheated. No payment.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ab-khichdi.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.khichdi|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.khichdi-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.khichdi:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Birbal's Khichdi","text":"बादशाह, जो थके हुए थे और ठीक से सोच नहीं पा रहे थे, मान गए। उस आदमी को खाली हाथ भेज दिया गया। बीरबल एक शब्द भी नहीं बोले — और अगले दिन दरबार में भी नहीं आए।","lang":"hi","body":"The Emperor, who was tired and not thinking clearly, agreed. The man was sent away with nothing. Birbal said not one word — and did not come to court the next day.","art":"art/story/sm/ab-khichdi.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.khichdi|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.khichdi-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.khichdi:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Birbal's Khichdi","text":"जब बादशाह ने उन्हें बुलवाया, तो बीरबल ने जवाब भिजवाया कि वे शाही दोपहर के खाने के लिए खिचड़ी पका रहे हैं और उसे छोड़कर बिल्कुल नहीं आ सकते। अकबर उत्सुक भी थे और अब तक उन्हें अच्छी-खासी भूख भी लग आई थी, इसलिए वे खुद देखने पहुँचे।","lang":"hi","body":"When the Emperor sent for him, Birbal replied that he was cooking khichdi for the royal lunch and could not possibly leave it. Akbar, curious and by now quite hungry, came to see for himself.","art":"art/story/sm/ab-khichdi.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.khichdi|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.khichdi-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.khichdi:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Birbal's Khichdi","text":"आँगन में बीरबल एक छोटी सी आग के पास बैठे थे। उस आग से बहुत ऊपर, एक खंभे से पूरे चार फीट की ऊँचाई पर, खिचड़ी की हाँडी लटक रही थी।","lang":"hi","body":"In the courtyard Birbal sat beside a small fire. High above it, dangling from a pole a good four feet up, hung the pot of khichdi.","art":"art/story/sm/ab-khichdi.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.khichdi|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.khichdi-6":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.khichdi:6","title":"Read it in Hindi · Birbal's Khichdi","text":"\"बीरबल, हाँडी आग से चार फ़ुट ऊपर है। वह खिचड़ी कभी नहीं पकेगी।\" बीरबल ने कहा, \"बिल्कुल पकेगी, जहाँपनाह। अगर एक मील दूर खिड़की में जलता हुआ दीया रात भर झील में खड़े आदमी को गरमाहट दे सकता है — तो यह आग मेरा दोपहर का खाना ज़रूर पका सकती है।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Birbal. The pot is four feet above the flame. That khichdi will never cook.\" \"Of course it will, Jahanpanah,\" said Birbal. \"If a lamp in a window a mile away can warm a man standing in a lake all night — then this fire can certainly cook my lunch.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ab-khichdi.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.khichdi|h6","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.crows-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.crows:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Many Crows in the Kingdom?","text":"अकबर महल की दीवार पर कौवों को आपस में लड़ते देख रहे थे, तभी उनके मन में एक विचार आया। उन्होंने पूछा, \"बीरबल, हमारे राज्य में कुल कितने कौवे हैं?\"","lang":"hi","body":"Akbar was watching crows squabble on the palace wall when a thought struck him. \"Birbal,\" he said. \"How many crows are there in my kingdom?\"","art":"art/story/sm/ab-crows.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.crows|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.crows-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.crows:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Many Crows in the Kingdom?","text":"यह एक ऐसा सवाल था जिसका कोई जवाब नहीं हो सकता था। पूरा दरबार मुस्कुरा उठा, क्योंकि इस बार सबको पक्का यकीन था कि बीरबल फँस गया है।","lang":"hi","body":"It was the sort of question that has no answer. The court smiled, because for once they were sure Birbal was finished.","art":"art/story/sm/ab-crows.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.crows|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.crows-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.crows:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Many Crows in the Kingdom?","text":"\"पंचानवे हज़ार चार सौ तिरेसठ, जहाँपनाह।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Ninety-five thousand, four hundred and sixty-three, Jahanpanah.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ab-crows.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.crows|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ab.crows-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ab.crows:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · How Many Crows in the Kingdom?","text":"\"तो फिर ज़्यादा कौवे पड़ोसी राज्य से अपने रिश्तेदारों से मिलने आए हैं, जहाँपनाह।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Then the extra crows are visiting relatives from the neighbouring kingdom, Jahanpanah.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ab-crows.jpg","route":"#/story/ab.crows|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Akbar & Birbal"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.ganesha-race-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.ganesha-race:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race Around the World","text":"एक बार एक ऋषि कैलाश पर सोने का एक अकेला आम लेकर आए — ज्ञान का फल, जो सिर्फ़ एक ही व्यक्ति के लिए था। शिव और पार्वती के दो बेटे थे: गोल-मटोल और विचारशील गणेश, और तेज़-तर्रार और जोशीले कार्तिकेय।","lang":"hi","body":"A sage once brought a single golden mango to Kailash — a fruit of wisdom, meant for one person only. Shiva and Parvati had two sons: Ganesha, round and thoughtful, and Kartikeya, quick and fierce.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-ganesha-race.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.ganesha-race|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.ganesha-race-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.ganesha-race:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race Around the World","text":"\"आम एक है और तुम दो,\" शिव ने कहा। \"तो फिर — एक दौड़ हो जाए। जो पूरी दुनिया का चक्कर लगाकर सबसे पहले यहाँ वापस लौटेगा, यह आम उसी को मिलेगा।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"There is one mango and two of you,\" said Shiva. \"So — a race. Whoever goes around the whole world and returns here first may have it.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ka-ganesha-race.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.ganesha-race|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.ganesha-race-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.ganesha-race:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race Around the World","text":"बात पूरी होने से पहले ही, कार्तिकेय अपने मोर पर सवार होकर पहाड़ों के पार निकल गए। गणेश ने अपनी छोटी-छोटी टाँगों की तरफ़ देखा, और उस नन्हे-से चूहे को देखा जिसकी वे सवारी करते थे। फिर वे बैठ गए और सोचने लगे।","lang":"hi","body":"Kartikeya leapt onto his peacock and was gone over the mountains before the sentence was finished. Ganesha looked down at his own short legs, and at the very small mouse he rode. Then he sat down and thought.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-ganesha-race.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.ganesha-race|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.ganesha-race-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.ganesha-race:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race Around the World","text":"गणेश खड़े हुए, धीरे-धीरे अपने माता-पिता के पास गए, और उनके चारों ओर पूरा चक्कर लगाया। एक बार। दो बार। तीन बार। फिर उन्होंने सिर झुकाया और अपना हाथ आगे बढ़ा दिया।","lang":"hi","body":"Ganesha stood up, walked slowly to his mother and father, and walked all the way around them. Once. Twice. Three times. Then he bowed and held out his hand.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-ganesha-race.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.ganesha-race|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.ganesha-race-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.ganesha-race:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Race Around the World","text":"\"मेरी पूरी दुनिया तो यहीं है,\" उन्होंने कहा। \"मैंने इसके तीन चक्कर लगा लिए हैं।\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"My whole world is right here,\" he said. \"I have been around it three times.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ka-ganesha-race.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.ganesha-race|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.hanuman-leap-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.hanuman-leap:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Hanuman's Leap","text":"सीता को समंदर पार लंका ले जाया जा चुका था। वानरों की सेना धरती की आखिरी चट्टान पर खड़ी होकर सौ मील फैले खुले समंदर को देख रही थी, और उनमें से हर कोई जानता था कि वे इसे पार नहीं कर सकते।","lang":"hi","body":"Sita had been carried away across the water to Lanka. The army of vanaras stood on the last rock of the mainland and looked at a hundred miles of open sea, and every one of them knew they could not cross it.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-hanuman-leap.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.hanuman-leap|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.hanuman-leap-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.hanuman-leap:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Hanuman's Leap","text":"हनुमान सबसे पीछे चुपचाप बैठे थे। बचपन में वे सूरज को आम समझकर उसकी ओर उछल पड़े थे, और इसके बदले उन्हें नीचे गिरा दिया गया था — और उस गिरने के साथ ही वे भूल गए थे कि वे क्या कुछ कर सकते थे।","lang":"hi","body":"Hanuman sat at the back, saying nothing. As a child he had leapt at the sun thinking it was a mango, and been struck down for it — and along with the fall he had lost the memory of what he could do.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-hanuman-leap.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.hanuman-leap|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.hanuman-leap-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.hanuman-leap:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Hanuman's Leap","text":"\"क्या तुम नहीं जानते कि तुम कौन हो?\" जामवंत ने कहा। \"पवनपुत्र! तुम चलना सीखने से पहले सूरज की ओर छलांग लगा चुके थे। इस पूरे तट पर तुम सबसे शक्तिशाली हो, और तुम यहाँ सबसे पीछे बैठे हो!\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"Do you not know what you are?\" said Jambavan. \"Son of the wind. You leapt at the sun before you could walk. You are the strongest creature on this shore, and you are sitting at the back.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ka-hanuman-leap.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.hanuman-leap|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.hanuman-leap-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.hanuman-leap:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · Hanuman's Leap","text":"और सुनते-सुनते हनुमान का आकार बढ़ने लगा। वे समंदर किनारे के पहाड़ पर चढ़े, और उनके पैरों के नीचे की चट्टान चटक गई। उन्होंने दूर क्षितिज की ओर देखा। और छलांग लगा दी।","lang":"hi","body":"And as he listened, Hanuman began to grow. He climbed the mountain at the water's edge, and the rock cracked under his feet. He looked at the horizon. And he jumped.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-hanuman-leap.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.hanuman-leap|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.hanuman-leap-5":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.hanuman-leap:5","title":"Read it in Hindi · Hanuman's Leap","text":"वे इतनी ऊँचाई पर गए कि पहाड़ के पेड़ उखड़कर उनके पीछे-पीछे उड़ने लगे, और उनके नीचे का समंदर एक चमकती हुई सड़क जैसा सपाट हो गया। बीच समंदर में उन्हें विश्राम देने के लिए पानी से एक पर्वत ऊपर उठा। हनुमान ने आदर से उसे छुआ, धन्यवाद दिया, और आगे बढ़ते चले गए।","lang":"hi","body":"He went so high the trees on the mountain were torn up behind him and flew along in his wake, and the sea beneath him flattened into a bright road. Somewhere over the middle of it a mountain rose out of the water to offer him a rest. He touched it politely, thanked it, and kept going.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-hanuman-leap.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.hanuman-leap|h5","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.buddha-mustard-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.buddha-mustard:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mustard Seed","text":"\"किसा गोतमी नाम की एक औरत का इकलौता बच्चा चल बसा। वह यह बात मानने को तैयार ही नहीं थी। वह बच्चे को उठाए पूरे शहर में घूमी और हर एक इंसान से उसे वापस लाने की दवा माँगती रही, पर सबने मुँह मोड़ लिया — आखिरकार एक बूढ़े आदमी ने कहा: \\\"बुद्ध के पास जाओ।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"A woman called Kisa Gotami lost her only child. She would not accept it. She carried him through the town asking every single person for medicine to bring him back, and everyone turned away — until one old man said: \"Go to the Buddha.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ka-buddha-mustard.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.buddha-mustard|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.buddha-mustard-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.buddha-mustard:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mustard Seed","text":"\"\\\"मैं तुम्हारी मदद कर सकता हूँ,\\\" बुद्ध ने कहा। \\\"मेरे लिए एक मुट्ठी सरसों के दाने ले आओ।\\\" वह दौड़ने को मुड़ी। \\\"लेकिन वो ऐसे घर से आने चाहिए,\\\" उन्होंने कहा, \\\"जहाँ कभी किसी की मौत न हुई हो।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"\"I can help you,\" said the Buddha. \"Bring me a handful of mustard seed.\" She turned to run. \"But it must come from a house,\" he said, \"where nobody has ever died.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ka-buddha-mustard.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.buddha-mustard|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.buddha-mustard-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.buddha-mustard:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mustard Seed","text":"\"वह पहले घर पहुँची। उन्होंने खुशी-खुशी उसे सरसों दे दी — भारत के हर रसोईघर में सरसों होती ही है। \\\"और क्या इस घर में किसी की मौत हुई है?\\\" उसने पूछा। उस औरत के चेहरे का रंग बदल गया। \\\"मेरे पति की। पिछली बसंत में।\\\"\"","lang":"hi","body":"She went to the first house. They gladly offered her mustard seed — every kitchen in India has mustard seed. \"And has anyone died in this house?\" she asked. The woman's face changed. \"My husband. Last spring.\"","art":"art/story/sm/ka-buddha-mustard.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.buddha-mustard|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.buddha-mustard-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.buddha-mustard:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mustard Seed","text":"\"एक के बाद एक, घर-घर। सरसों तो हर किसी के पास थी। पर ऐसा घर किसी का न था जहाँ कभी मौत न आई हो। कहीं दादी। कहीं भाई। कहीं नन्हा बच्चा। कहीं कोई दोस्त। शाम होते-होते वह पूरा शहर नाप चुकी थी और उसके हाथ खाली थे।\"","lang":"hi","body":"House after house after house. Everyone had mustard seed. Nobody had a house that death had never entered. A grandmother. A brother. A baby. A friend. By evening she had walked the whole town and her hands were empty.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-buddha-mustard.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.buddha-mustard|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.buddha-mustard-4":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.buddha-mustard:4","title":"Read it in Hindi · The Mustard Seed","text":"\"वह सड़क किनारे बैठ गई। और दूसरों के दुख-दर्द से भरे उस लंबे दिन में, उसे पता भी न चला कि कब वह अकेली नहीं रही थी।\"","lang":"hi","body":"She sat down at the edge of the road. And somewhere in that long day of other people's losses, without noticing it happening, she had stopped being alone.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-buddha-mustard.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.buddha-mustard|h4","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.mahavira-elephant-0":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.mahavira-elephant:0","title":"Read it in Hindi · Six Blind Men and an Elephant","text":"जन्म से अंधे छह आदमियों को एक हाथी के पास लाया गया और बताने को कहा गया कि वह कैसा होता है। उन सबने हाथ आगे बढ़ाया और उसके अलग-अलग हिस्से को छुआ।","lang":"hi","body":"Six men who had been blind from birth were brought to an elephant and asked to say what it was like. Each of them reached out and touched a different part.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-mahavira-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.mahavira-elephant|h0","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.mahavira-elephant-1":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.mahavira-elephant:1","title":"Read it in Hindi · Six Blind Men and an Elephant","text":"\"एक मोटा साँप,\" सूँड पकड़े हुए आदमी ने कहा। \"एक पंखा,\" कान के पास वाले ने कहा। \"पेड़ का तना,\" पैर को बाहों में घेरे आदमी ने कहा। \"एक दीवार।\" \"एक भाला।\" \"एक रस्सी,\" आखिरी आदमी ने कहा, जिसके हाथ पूँछ लगी थी।","lang":"hi","body":"\"A thick snake,\" said the one holding the trunk. \"A fan,\" said the one at the ear. \"A tree trunk,\" said the one with his arms round a leg. \"A wall.\" \"A spear.\" \"A rope,\" said the last one, who had found the tail.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-mahavira-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.mahavira-elephant|h1","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.mahavira-elephant-2":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.mahavira-elephant:2","title":"Read it in Hindi · Six Blind Men and an Elephant","text":"उनमें बहस हुई। फिर वे चिल्लाने लगे। हर एक को लग रहा था कि वही सही है, क्योंकि हर कोई सही था भी।","lang":"hi","body":"They argued. Then they shouted. Each of them could feel that he was right, because each of them was.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-mahavira-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.mahavira-elephant|h2","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]},"hp-ka.mahavira-elephant-3":{"src":"passage:hi:story:ka.mahavira-elephant:3","title":"Read it in Hindi · Six Blind Men and an Elephant","text":"जैन गुरु इसे अनेकांतवाद कहते हैं — यानी कई पहलू होना। सच के इतने पहलू होते हैं कि कोई भी एक इंसान उन सबको एक साथ नहीं समझ सकता। तुमने जो छुआ वह सच है। बस, वही पूरा सच नहीं है।","lang":"hi","body":"The Jain teachers call this anekantavada — many-sidedness. Truth has more sides than any one person can hold at once. What you touched is real. It is simply not all of it.","art":"art/story/sm/ka-mahavira-elephant.jpg","route":"#/story/ka.mahavira-elephant|h3","cta":"Read it in Hindi","why":"A story you can read in Hindi","facts":[["From","Great Stories"],["On the path","Padhna — Reading"]]}});
